# HTML and identity

**Prerequisites:** [Write markup](/docs/how-to/write-markup/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Update the UI](/docs/how-to/update-the-ui/).

Datastar patches match existing DOM. A fragment must reuse an `id` that already
exists in the document. Changing the `id` between render and patch looks like a
missing target, not a “refresh”.

Prefer semantic elements (`button`, `label`, headings) over generic `div`s with
click handlers. Accessible names (`alt`, visible text, `aria-*` when needed)
survive morphs only if they stay in the HTML you return.

List rows need per-item ids (`row-12`), not a single `#list` that replaces
unrelated siblings.

**Related:** [Tags](/docs/reference/language/tags/).
